# Root crontab for BYTE by ACE.
#
# Deliberately empty. An hourly "echo 3 > drop_caches && swapoff -a && swapon -a"
# used to live here. It was removed because it made the box worse:
#
#   drop_caches  throws away the page cache and dentries every hour, so the
#                next requests page the kernel to fetch them again - pure CPU
#                and latency cost, no throughput gain. It also makes memory
#                look "free" while the kernel is actually warm.
#   swapoff/swapon  forces all 433 MB of zram to be decompressed back into RAM
#                and then re-compressed, which stalls every process touching
#                swapped pages for the whole cycle. Under memory pressure that
#                is exactly when the stall hurts most.
#
# Leave the kernel's own reclaim alone: it already evicts cold pages on
# demand, and zram is meant to stay warm.
#
# ci_check_packages fails the build if either command comes back.
